      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find $\\mathbf{x}$, if $4\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}36 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -38\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{x} & =\\mathbf{b} \\\\ 6\\mathbf{x} & =\\mathbf{b}-4\\mathbf{a} \\\\ \\mathbf{x} & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\mathbf{b}-4\\mathbf{a}) \\\\ \\mathbf{x} & =\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}36 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -38\\end{bmatrix}-4\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\right) \\\\ \\mathbf{x} & =\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -42\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\mathbf{x} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
